    correctness_result: "6 examples, 6 passed (KAT vectors incl. ASCII
      letters/digits/control chars, multibyte UTF-8 across all four
      encoding-length classes (1/2/3/4-byte), invalid-codepoint edge cases
      incl. negative/above-U+10FFFF/surrogate-range collapsing to empty on
      both sides, surrogate-boundary discrimination, single-codepoint
      corruption discrimination, determinism check, 100-vector shared-logic
      bulk differential loop covering every encoding-length class plus every
      rejection branch, 2026-08-18)"
    c_status: retained_as_test_oracle
    perf_status: "PERF FINDING — pure-Simple char_from_code measured ~3.5x
      the C oracle (interpreter dispatch to `char::from_u32`) over the
      100-vector bulk corpus (simple_us=9939, c_us=2811, single run,
      tree-walk interpreter via `bin/simple test`, 2026-08-18), above the
      plan's 2x threshold. Recorded honestly, not hidden — same
      interpreter-lane caveat as prior PERF findings (bin/simple test
      hard-defaults to the interpreter, not the JIT/native engine ordinary
      programs run on)."
    perf_measured: >
      100 shared branch-covering codepoints (seeded LCG cycling through all
