      the C source directly when running under `bin/simple test`
      (tree-walk interpreter). No prior pure-Simple counterpart existed
      outside string_core.spl, so one was written:
      src/lib/common/encoding/byte_char.spl reimplements the UTF-8 byte math
      directly (1-byte encoding for 0x00..0x7F, 2-byte 0xC2/0xC3-lead
      encoding for 0x80..0xFF) using u64 bit ops, and uses `rt_bytes_to_text`
      only as a raw byte-array-to-text memcpy primitive (the same
      non-algorithmic role that extern already plays inside
      string_core.spl's own char_from_code_inline, per C-MIG-0027), not as
