      src/runtime/*.h` returns zero hits); this is a pure-Rust-interpreter
      extern, same kind as C-MIG-0029/0030 (no_c_implementation_rust_only_
      extern), unlike C-MIG-0027/0028's runtime_native.c-backed externs.
    correctness_spec: test/01_unit/lib/common/numeric_round_floor_crosslang_spec.spl
    correctness_result: "6 examples, 6 passed (KAT vectors incl. positive
      AND negative fractions, zero, negative-zero preservation,
      domain-boundary coverage (+-infinity, NaN, large-magnitude
      1.0e20/-1.0e20 beyond i64 range), single-bit corruption
      discrimination, determinism check, 100-vector shared-logic bulk
      differential loop with forced zero/negative-zero/+-1.0e20/sign-flip/
      half-offset boundary values at fixed moduli, 2026-08-18)"
    c_status: no_c_implementation_rust_only_extern
    perf_status: "PERF FINDING — pure-Simple floor_f64 measured ~2.65x the
      Rust hardware-floor oracle over the 100-vector bulk corpus
      (simple_us=1252, c_us=473, single run, tree-walk interpreter via
      `bin/simple test`, 2026-08-18), above the plan's 2x threshold.
      Recorded honestly, not hidden -- same interpreter-lane caveat as
      prior PERF findings (bin/simple test hard-defaults to the
      interpreter, not the JIT/native engine ordinary programs run on)."
    perf_measured: >
      100 shared branch-covering x values (seeded LCG cycling through
      0.0..1000.0 in 0.001 steps, plus forced boundary values at fixed
      moduli: 0.0 at i % 19 == 0, -0.0 at i % 17 == 0, 1.0e20 at i % 13 ==
      0, -1.0e20 at i % 11 == 0, sign-flip at i % 7 == 0, half-offset at
      i % 5 == 0), 2026-08-18: simple_us=1252 c_us=473, ratio ~2.65x.
    shared_corpus: 100
    fixed_perf_bugs: []
    domain_bug_note: >
      Bug found and fixed while writing this spec (not filed as a
      standalone bug doc -- fixed inline before landing, per the
      sqrt/cbrt precedent of catching domain bugs during spec writing):
      an early unguarded version of floor_f64 used a bare `x as i64`
      round-trip, which is undefined/saturating for magnitudes outside
      i64's ~9.22e18 range and for +-infinity, corrupting those inputs
      instead of returning them unchanged. Fixed by adding a 2^52
      integrality-threshold guard (every f64 at or beyond that magnitude
      already has zero fractional part) that short-circuits to the
      identity before the cast; re-verified against the oracle across the
      full KAT + domain-boundary + 100-vector bulk-loop suite above.

